    "title": "Refactoring Tips: Small Steps, Big Impact 🛠️",
    "content": "Hey devs! 🚀

If you're looking to improve your code's clarity and maintainability, small, testable refactors are your best friend. Instead of rewriting entire modules, focus on incremental changes that make your code more readable and easier to test.

💡 **Pro tip:** Always check for naming inconsistencies and cohesion issues. A well-named function or variable can save hours of debugging later.

Here's a quick example:

```js
// Before
function calc(a, b) { return a + b; }

// After
function addNumbers(x, y) { return x + y; }
```

This tiny change makes the code more expressive and easier to understand.

Remember, the goal isn't to make everything perfect at once — it's to make it better over time. 🛠️

What's your favorite refactoring pattern? Share below! 💬"
}

