    "content": "Hey devs! 💻

If you're working on a large project and importing modules locally, consider using `@` as an alias for `src/` in your `tsconfig.json` or `jsconfig.json`. It makes imports cleaner and faster to type.

Example:
```json
{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "baseUrl": ".",
    "paths": {
      "@/*": ["src/*"]
    }
  }
}
```

Then you can import like:
```ts
import { Component } from '@/components/Component';
```

This also helps with tree-shaking and build performance. Want to try it out? Let me know and I can help you set it up! 🚀"
